---
import '../styles/design-reference.css';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import distribution from '../data/distribution.json';
const endpoint=distribution.mcp.url;
---
<BaseLayout title="Build with Krigsvold and an agent" description="Connect to the independent read-only Krigsvold MCP and retrieve the builder method, grammar, patterns and actual APIs.">
<article class="design-reference">
<header><p class="reference-label">Krigsvold · Agent access</p><h1>Build with the language.</h1><p>The MCP serves public design knowledge. No account, API key or local server download is required. Every composition remains subject to the documented experimental limits.</p></header>
<section><h2>Connect the MCP</h2><pre tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="MCP endpoint"><code>{endpoint}</code></pre><p>Read-only tools: <code>get_manifest</code>, <code>search_guidance</code> and <code>get_reference</code>. The server also exposes exact resources, source commits and content hashes. It has no access to the workbench database, drafts or write operations.</p></section>
<section><h2>Existing connections</h2><p>The canonical endpoint is now <code>{endpoint}</code>. Existing clients at <code>https://krigsvoldtheme.dev/mcp</code> continue to work.</p></section>
<section><h2>ChatGPT</h2><p>Open Plugins, select the plus button and Add custom MCP server. Enter this endpoint, choose No authentication, review the connection, create the plugin and install it. Select it with @ in a new conversation. Account and workspace permissions apply.</p></section>
<section><h2>Claude</h2><p>Open Customize → Connectors, add a custom Web connector and paste the endpoint. Choose No sign in, then enable the connector for the conversation. Team and Enterprise owners may need to add it first.</p><h3>Claude Code</h3><pre tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Claude Code setup"><code>claude mcp add --transport http krigsvold-design-language https://krigsvolddesign.dev/mcp</code></pre></section>
<section><h2>Retrieve the builder method</h2><p>Call <code>get_manifest</code> and confirm <code>family=krigsvold</code>. Retrieve <code>builder-skill</code> and <code>grammar</code> with <code>get_reference</code>. Search for the task, retrieve complete patterns and actual component contracts, then build and verify the whole interaction. The method is available through MCP without downloading a skill. MCP itself does not install persistent skills.</p><p><a href="/agents/krigsvold-builder.zip" download>Optional builder skill ZIP</a> · <a href="/agents/krigsvold-agent-tools.tar.gz" download>Offline stdio MCP and skill</a></p></section>
<section><h2>Package publication</h2><div class="reference-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Package availability"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Package</th><th scope="col">Version</th><th scope="col">Availability</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.values(distribution.packages).map(p=><tr><th scope="row">{p.name}</th><td>{p.version}</td><td>{p.published ? 'Published · next · experimental' : 'Publication pending'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>Install exact versions deliberately. The existing latest tags remain unchanged. Canonical guidance snapshots retain their original review-time status; this table records release availability separately.</p></section>
<section><h2>Evidence and limits</h2><p>SDK checks cover modern and legacy HTTP negotiation, tools and resources, source hashes, family isolation, invalid input and unavailable references. Actual installation inside a particular ChatGPT or Claude account is a separate check. Manual assistive-technology review, RTL, compact density and sustained consumer use remain open.</p><p><a href="/design-language/">Grammar and patterns</a> · <a href="/design-system/">Installed package reference</a></p></section>
</article>
</BaseLayout>
